[
  {
    "episode_id": 51012,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/5/1/51012.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 0,
    "turn_text": "Hi everybody. I'm Patricia Duff and welcome to the Common Good. We're going to have a little bit of a delay before we have our Congresswoman on. We're going to find out how long that will be in the meantime. I just want to welcome and acknowledge a few of our honorables and our VIPs in our audience because we've got quite a few notables. We're expecting as our honorary advisory board members, Congresswoman Jane Harmon, Alan Patrickoff, Byron Wien, Kate Kopplevitz, Stan Schuman, a couple of honorables, Gillian Sorensen, Amanda Burton, Juju Chang from the press, also from the press, Judith Miller and Nancy Collins. And a lot of past speakers and hosts like Kim Tae-Pao, Bill Hubbard, Richard Solomon, Karen Meale, Debbie Bancroft, Jonathan Barnett, and Richard Gordon. And I'm happy to have our young change maker award sponsor, Sharon Patrick, and an ASA awardee, Henry Shelfont, for Freedom of Expression. And of course, there are so many activists and donors and engaged citizens on the call to name you all. So we're going to hopefully just talk amongst ourselves while we wait for Katie to join us. But I did want you to meet our moderator today who's also on our honorary advisory board, Tom Rogers. He's going to lead the conversation. He's a media pioneer editor at large at Newsweek. And most importantly, a great friend of the common good. You probably are familiar with many of the corners of the communications industry that Tom has shaped as he revolutionized political and business news coverage worldwide through the creation of CNBC and MSNBC. But Tom has operated the nexus of media technology and public policy for more than three decades. and his latest company, Engine Media, joined the NASDAQ board with the call letters G-A-M-E game. Guess what they do? In just the past couple of weeks, so congratulations to you, Tom, for that. And thank you so much for monitoring this important conversation. So I'm happy to see you, Tom. Looking very serious.",
