    "turn_idx": 46,
    "turn_text": "Well, most of the news channels are suffering from Donald Trump withdrawal. Well, many of us may be happy with what Twitter did in taking them out of the minute by minute daily conversation. News channels are really suffering in terms of the decline of their audience since his departure from the scene in terms of being in everybody's face and every news cycle. The more the other challenge of news channels today is the one that Netflix and Disney Plus and Hulu and all of them have created by most entertainment programming going to streaming. And what that has caused, of course, is an acceleration and cord cutting and fewer and fewer people taking the cable and satellite bundle. And why that's important is that most of the revenue that news channels get comes from the fees paid by every cable and satellite home. So news channels at any given time may have less than 1% of television homes watching them, but they get substantial fees from 100% of cable and satellite homes. And it's a number of those homes shrink and what's expected to be Market shrinkage as streaming services continue to gain popularity and fewer and fewer people see any reason to pay $100 a month for cable or satellite. That's a significant overhang on the economics of news channels. So you're beginning to see some creative finance enter the new space just this week BuzzFeed going",
