    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/5/1/51012.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 53,
    "turn_text": "It's a good point. I think most cable networks as audience has declined and ratings have declined. They have tried to shoehorn in more spots. Which in my mind is self defeating because that chases more and more audience away less so in the new space more when it comes to them doing that on entertainment channels and people get increasingly frustrated and go to non commercial streaming services. But yes, that is definitely a phenomenon. And news channels in their current form skew older. Most news audience is 60 and older. And that's another thing where advertisers don't pay as much as they do for a 25 to 54 audience. And so that's an additional overhang. So reinventing the news model is something that has to happen.",
