  {
    "episode_id": 51012,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/5/1/51012.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 129,
    "turn_text": "Well, I think this is a fundamental underlying point that you're raking, which is that oversight and accountability are not things that we just need to do when the other party is in power. This is fundamentally not just about which political parties in power, it's about the balance of power. And so Congress's ability to ask questions of the executive and to get answers, Congress's ability to investigate whether laws that we have passed are being followed. Those are things that ought to concern us regardless of which party is in charge and my colleagues Ted Lu and Adam Schiff and others have been giving thought to and I think Ted has a bill on this to try to beef up and streamline the process. You know what I have a hearing today and I ask the most important entity is hearing about a coal ash plant in Puerto Rico in a very low income community, and it's contributing to rates of cancer that are one in four. If you can imagine that in proximity to this plant. And we asked the entity responsible for the plant to testify. And they said yes. And then they said no, which is not a thing. I just want to be clear. If you say you're coming to Congress, you better show up. So they said yes, and then they said no. And today, I made very clear in the hearing, I am absolutely prepared to subpoena them if necessary. But when companies know that if they stall, the Congress will run out and the other party may take control, then those subpoenas lose a lot of their effectiveness. And so I think we always should be inviting companies and witnesses and trying to get them to come voluntarily, but when we have to use our subpoena power, These are time sensitive issues. People are dying because of this coal ash plant and adding a year or two to having a discussion about who's responsible and what can we do, real lives will be lost in that time. So I think it's important to remind people, these are not just about esoteric legal maneuvers. Real lives are at stake when Congress can't get answers.",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_01",
    "inferred_speaker_name": null,
    "inferred_speaker_role": null,
