    "turn_text": "Very good, very good. All right, let's turn to infrastructure since I'm sure you've been involved in countless conversations about how to thread this needle here. There's a so-called bipartisan compromise related to what is known as traditional infrastructure with some new elements that we were talking about before you got on like broadband and new additions to traditional infrastructure. And Biden, of course, first said that he supported it and seemed to suggest it was tied to the so-called human infrastructure elements, having to be tied through reconciliation process, then he backed away from that, though it doesn't seem as if congressional leadership is backed away from tying the two. You come from a very swing district. You're the first Democrat ever elected from that district. This has to be one where I got to believe you understand the political value in Biden getting through a bipartisan compromise on something that there is that much support publicly for. What do you think the right way to handle this is in terms of these things being tied, not tied, sequencing, et cetera?",
